## Result: NOT SECURED — with a structural finding that decides the contract

**`e2-trestle` cannot be secured by surviving to its secure wave.** `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1095`, `autoSecureWaveForRun`, returns `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` while `twist.baron && !this.baronBeaten` — so with the wave-12 railcar alive, `maybeSecureRun` never fires, `now.pendingSecure` never appears, and `SECURE_CHOICE` is never accepted. The only door is `bossKillSecuresRun` (`:251`): all three railcar components dead, `bossRemaining === 0`.

That also corrects my own generation-8 notebook entry, which recorded that the secure gate has no defeat condition. It has one on every contract declaring a baron — I read `maybeSecureRun` but not the value it reads.

