The progression is worth reading: v1 built the textbook fort on the stake and only one of its four turrets was inside 16 wu of the railcar's fixed line at x = 0. v2 moved the turrets onto the rail shoulder and rode deeper, but a phase-gated ladder stalled forever on one unplaceable slot at (9,−13) — it fought the whole contract on three turrets. v3 made the ladder failure-tolerant and landed the full fort (4 turrets, 6 beacons, hero untouched at 175/175 into wave 11) — and moved the result three seconds, because survival was never the thing that ends this run.

**Winnability:** undecided, and the wall is boss damage in the map, not the grammar or the economy. Survival is solved and gold is in surplus; four capped turrets and six capped beacons do not finish an `hpScale: 12.5` three-component railcar during the dozen-odd seconds it spends in range. I did not spend the second attempt — an identical retry could not close a gap I could name, and the wall was closing.

